  [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Summary\n\nTermux Python 3.14 can hard-crash on `curl_cffi` 0.16 (missing libc++ symbol). Make the import optional and fall back to `requests` so deepcli/DeepForge can start.\n\n**Status:** 🟢 **Merge candidate** (small, targeted)  \n**Disposition:** Best near-term deepcli reliability win; base already `master-staging`.  \n**Base:** `master-staging`  \n**Implements:** CE-09 / TER-13\n\n### Changes\n- Try `curl_cffi.requests`; on failure alias to `requests` + one-line stderr warning\n- Relax session type annotations to `Any` where required\n\n### Non-goals\n- Fixing upstream `curl_cffi` wheels for Android\n- DeepForge launcher policy (PR #9)\n\n### Validation\n```bash\npython -c \"from deepcli.core import get_session; print('ok')\"\n# DeepForge / codex_bridge menu → deepcli should enter without import crash\n```\nIf live CLI is `~/deepcli/` outside the monorepo, apply the same import block there.\n\n### Agent notes\n- **Summary-Editor:** `grok-archw1z`\n- Related: PR #9 (DeepForge)\n"[m[1;37m,[m
